00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:35.809
So the first thing, Season 4 Episode titles.

00:00:35.809 --> 00:00:42.179
Episode 1 is called Two Swords, Episode 2
is called The Lion and The Lion and The Rose,

00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:47.570
Episode 3 is called Breaker of Chains and
Episode 4 is called Oathkeeper.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.539
What do all of those mean in terms of the
story, here’s where things might get a little

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:51.539
spoilery.

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:54.670
So just turn the volume down for a sec if
you don’t want to know anything.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:59.879
The episode 1 title Two Swords is a reference
to the melting down of Ned Stark’s two-handed

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:03.010
valyrian greatsword Ice into two smaller blades.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.040
We saw an image of this in the trailer.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.090
One of the blades is named Widow’s Wail
and is given to Joffrey as a wedding present

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:14.020
and the other larger blade is named Oathkeeper
and is given the Jaime until he gives it to

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.020
Brienne.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:18.120
The Episode 2 title The Lion and The Rose
is all purple wedding.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:24.300
I won’t mention the crazy spoiler here,
but the wedding ceremony and the wedding reception

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.410
will take up the entire episode.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:29.050
This will be one of the first major events
of the season.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.650
If you didn’t see it, the showrunners said
that there would be multiple Red Wedding level

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.490
climaxes this season, not just one.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.350
So Episode 2 will be the first one.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.030
I am planning on doing a couple videos just
for The Purple Wedding, because it’s going

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.180
to be awesome.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.260
The Episode 3 title is Breaker of Chains.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:52.730
Every title has multiple meanings but the
first that come to mind here are one, Tyrion’s

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:57.450
Chains after the last episode and two Daenerys
trying to break the slaves chains in Mereen.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.470
So one person is getting thrown in chains
and another group is coming out of chains.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.250
If you remember in the trailer we saw Tyrion
marching to his tribunal in chains and we

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.910
also saw Dany and her men at the beginning
of a battle.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.410
The breaking of those slaves chains could
come in a different episode from this battle

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.220
though.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.370
After she moves into this giant pyramid, also
from the trailer.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:20.740
It’s also possible that breaker of chains
could imply that some Maester chain’s could

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.980
be broken, but this seems like it will be
mostly a Dany Tyrion Episode.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.280
The Episode 4 title Oathkeeper is all about
the sword from Episode 1.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.010
But it’s name also kind of informs Brienne’s
quest to find Sansa who they think has been

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.010
kidnapped.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.840
There have actually been some behind the scenes
pics from these scenes.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.060
Look at Podrick smoking.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.230
I wonder where you buy cigarettes in Oldtown.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.900
You can turn the volume back up, spoilers
over.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.670
Now let’s talk Winds of Winter.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:48.530
